# AGENTS.md — Architectural Charter (`turbo-lean` [incl. `LeanNative`] ⟷ `lean-sys` ⟷ `orb`)

## 1. Symbiosis & Architectural Roles

`turbo-lean` (unifying `TurboLean` and `LeanNative`), `lean-sys`, and `orb` form a co-designed formal verification, native compilation, and systems runtime stack for Lean 4:

- **`turbo-lean` (`lean/TurboLean/` + `crates/turbo-lean/` — Incremental Verification, Zygote Elaboration & Counterexample Triage)**:
  Partitions Lean modules into topological dependency cones and sub-proof cuts, caches artifacts across content-addressed memory and persistent stores, orchestrates warm `Command.State` Zygote workers, exposes an MCP server (`turbo_fast_check`, `turbo_agent_step`, `turbo_audit_spec`, `turbo_check_decl`, `turbo_pr_verify`, `turbo_cluster_status`, `turbo_agent_analytics`) with structured counterexample triage (`CandidateBug | SpecTooStrong | ReferenceDiscrepancy`), and enforces an in-kernel soundness gate (`0 sorryAx`, `0 native_decide`, `0 trustCompiler`, statement pinning, and nested-inductive hygiene).
